runbooks/RUNNING_THE_LOOP.md:115:A BOUNCE lists each defect as its own point: what is wrong, where, and what done requires instead. The author fixes, reports the new head, and the reviewer re-checks the delta — not the whole branch again. If a prior review judged pinned tip X and the branch later moved to Y by appending commits, the re-check may be scoped to X..Y before any publish decision at Y.
